From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "AnyBook (ANAL-297)" <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY: stay loaded without an NVIDIA GPU (QEMU check)

Never shipped. scripts/kernel-nvidia-open-qemu-variant.sh builds nvidia.ko with this for the QEMU check (scripts/nvidia-open-guest-check.sh), which has no NVIDIA GPU: nvidia.ko then registers its character devices and device nodes as it does with an NVSwitch present, the shipped nvidia-modeset.ko and nvidia-drm.ko load on top, and the first ioctls run.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
index 850be3c..a429e31 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
@@ -1035,7 +1035,12 @@ static int __init nvidia_init_module(void)
     NvU32 count;
     NvBool warn_unprobed = NV_FALSE;
     nvidia_stack_t *sp = NULL;
-    const NvBool is_nvswitch_present = os_is_nvswitch_present();
+    /*
+     * AnyBook QEMU test build only, never shipped (kernel/patches/nvidia-open/test): stay loaded without an NVIDIA
+     * GPU, as NVIDIA's own code does when an NVSwitch is present, so that the QEMU check can load the shipped
+     * nvidia-modeset.ko and nvidia-drm.ko on top and issue the first ioctls.
+     */
+    const NvBool is_nvswitch_present = NV_TRUE;
     int num_pci_devices = 0, num_platform_devices = 0;
 
     nv_memdbg_init();
